{- | The functional calculus on `L⁰` for all cover maps $\varphi \colon \mathbb R^n \to \mathbb R$ (Theorem `thm:calc0`).

  * {l0calc}: the cover map $\varphi \colon (\mathrm L^0)^n \to \mathrm L^0$.
  * {l0calc-char}: for $\chi \in C_0$ it extends the functional calculus {fcalc} of `L`; {l0calc-coord}: $x_j(F) = F_j$;
    {l0calc-const}: a rational constant `q` goes to $q \cdot 1$ ({l0One}).
  * {l0calc-add}, {l0calc-neg}, {l0calc-join}, {l0calc-meet}, {l0calc-*q}: $\varphi \mapsto \varphi(F)$ is a homomorphism of Riesz spaces over `ℚ`.
  * {l0calc-mono}: transfer; {l0calc-comp}: composition.

  Construction for $\varphi(0) = 0$ (`l0calc0`, in `L0CalcHelpers`). For $f \in L^n$, $\varphi(f)$ is the limit in `L⁰` of $\varphi_k(f)$, where
  $\varphi_k = (\varphi \wedge k\|x\|_1) \vee (-k\|x\|_1) \in C_0$ ({clipApprox}); the net is Cauchy by `gauge-bound` because
  $\varphi_k \to \varphi$ uniformly on balls and $d_h$ only sees $|\cdot| \wedge h$.
  The map $f \mapsto \varphi(f)$ is locally uniformly continuous (`l0calc-preLU`): near $f_0$ the tails $(\|f\|_1 - M)^+$ are controlled by
  $d_h(f - f_0, 0)$, and $\varphi_k$ is uniformly continuous on balls. So it extends to $(\mathrm L^0)^n$.
  The laws hold on $L^n$ because approximants converging uniformly on balls converge in `L⁰` (`pre-limit`), and extend by density.

  General $\varphi$ (in `L0GenHelpers`): $\varphi(F) = \Psi_\varphi(1, F)$ with $\Psi_\varphi(t, x) = (\varphi(x) - \varphi(0)) + \varphi(0)(t \wedge 1)$
  (`homog`), which vanishes at `0`. The key fact is locality (`l0calc0-vanish`): if $D(t, x) = 0$ for $t \ge 1$, then $D(1, F) = 0$,
  since $1 = \lim_h \tau(h)$ and $|D_k(\tau(k/\eta + w), x)| \wedge k \le k \wedge \eta$ pointwise. The laws for $\vee$, $\wedge$ and composition
  follow because both sides agree for $t \ge 1$ (`l0calc0-local`).
-}

